Well, maybe we should explain what a stand-in is if we haven't before.

757
00:35:03.020 --> 00:35:09.480
So after you rehearse a scene with the actors, you bring in people to stand in for the actors

758
00:35:09.480 --> 00:35:12.580
while the crew sets the lights and the camera angles.

759
00:35:12.740 --> 00:35:16.840
And this is an opportunity for the cast to go and get their makeup fixed or change their

760
00:35:16.840 --> 00:35:20.440
outfit or any number of things, rehearse their lines.

761
00:35:20.440 --> 00:35:24.760
And then when we're ready to start rolling, the actors come back in and stand in their

762
00:35:24.760 --> 00:35:26.020
positions or sit at their desks.

763
00:35:26.240 --> 00:35:29.160
So Lori would stand in for all the women.

764
00:35:29.160 --> 00:35:32.340
And Stephen, her husband, would stand in for the men.

765
00:35:32.680 --> 00:35:35.980
But every once in a while, you'll see them pop up in the background of scenes.

766
00:35:36.080 --> 00:35:37.180
And that's what happened here.

767
00:35:37.180 --> 00:35:38.580
Yeah, they're wonderful.

768
00:35:38.580 --> 00:35:40.100
And we all became very close.

